    {
      "id": "WPW-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-short-norm-primes",
      "title": "Short-interval norm primes in an imaginary quadratic ray class",
      "hypotheses": "d is prime with d ≡ 3 mod 4 and d ≥ 100 (supplied by PRP-03); M ≥ 3 is an integer; B = 4dM²; X ≥ 1 and h are real numbers satisfying log B ≤ c√(log X) and exp(−c√(log X)) ≤ h ≤ 1. For the dyadic auxiliary-prime extraction at N = QS·q·d (QS > 0), 1 ≤ k ≤ r ≤ x⁵ and Y = (kb)⁸ with b = exp(L), L = x^ε.",
      "statement": "There exist absolute constants A, c, c′ > 0 such that the interval (X, X(1 + h)] contains at least c′hX / ((4dM²)^A log X) primes p represented as 4p = A₀² + dB₀² with M ∣ B₀ and 2M ∣ A₀ − 2 − B₀, equivalently p = ππ̄ for a unique π ∈ 𝒪_K with π − 1 ∈ M𝒪_K in K = ℚ(√(−d)). At h = 1 this gives at least Y^(9/10) such primes in (Y, 2Y]; discarding at most 20r³Y^(3/4) < Y^(9/10) candidates sharing an exceptional cyclotomic prime divisor through exponent r extracts two distinct auxiliary primes g₀ ≠ g₁ in [(kb)⁸, 2(kb)⁸] with disjoint exceptional divisor sets.",
      "definitions": [
        "imaginary quadratic integer ring 𝒪_K = ℤ[(1 + √(−d))/2]",
        "ray class group modulo M𝒪_K and density 2π/(√d M²)",
        "binary quadratic congruence representation of 4p",
        "effective exceptional-zero repulsion δ = c₉ / B^(A₁) (0 < c₉ ≤ 1)",
        "exceptional cyclotomic prime divisors through exponent r"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-short-norm-bound"
      ],
