      "correspondence": "In 𝒪_K = ℤ[(1+√(−d))/2], π = u + v(1+√(−d))/2 has 4ππ̄ = A₀² + dB₀² with A₀ = 2u + v, B₀ = v, and π − 1 ∈ M𝒪_K iff M ∣ B₀ and 2M ∣ A₀ − 2 − B₀. Injecting G into Cl(𝒪_K) × (𝒪_K/M𝒪_K) with Minkowski's bound h_K ≤ d ≤ 4d gives |G| ≤ 4dM² = B, while d ≥ 100 and M ≥ 3 make 1-mod-M𝒪_K generators unique and give ray-class density 2π/(√d M²). Character orthogonality combines hX, exceptional loss ≤ hX(1 − δ/2) for δ = c₉ / B^(A₁) (0 < c₉ ≤ 1), and summed Perron errors ≤ hXδ/4 before removing O(√X) prime powers and dividing by 4 log X; on [Y, 2Y] at most (3r + 1)(1 + 2r²(Y^(3/4) + 1)) ≤ 20r³Y^(3/4) < Y^(9/10) primes share an exceptional cyclotomic divisor.",
      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "review": "Hypotheses, binary quadratic congruences, Minkowski ray-class bound, cyclotomic exclusion and short-interval assembly audited against pinned Lean declarations."
