      "title": "Unconditional selection of each word’s level prime and window bounds",
      "hypotheses": "0 < ε < 1/52, c_s > 0, C_Y > 0 (C_Y = 9 on the global route), x ≥ x₀ (in particular x ≥ max(2, c_s^(−4))) with L = x^ε; d ≥ 100 prime with d ≡ 3 mod 4; N = QS·q·d > 0 divisible by d with log N ≤ 3x^(ε/5)(log x)²; 1 ≤ g_i ≤ exp(C_Y L); integers m ≥ x^(1/3) and f, k ≥ 1 with 1 ≤ V = fk ≤ x¹²; any two pre-assigned host primes strictly below X′ = exp(x^(ε/3)); D★ > 0, d_u★ > 0, Γ > 1 (and Γ ≥ 1 for the upper log bound), X_u = (D★ / d_u★)^(1/(fk)), T_u* = X_u Γ^(−2/(fk)), and c_s m L ≤ log T_u*.",
      "statement": "For M = N(g₀g₁)², every word u admits a prime T_u ∈ (T_u*, (1 + 1/(fk))T_u*] ⊆ [T_u*, (1 + 1/(fk))T_u*] distinct from both pre-assigned host primes below X′ = exp(x^(ε/3)), congruent to 1 modulo QS·q·d, with π_u ∈ 𝒪_E ∩ K satisfying π_u π̄_u = T_u and π_u − 1 ∈ N(g₀g₁)²𝒪_E. For every prime T_u in [T_u*, (1 + 1/(fk))T_u*] and Γ ≥ 1, d_u★ T_u^(fk) ≤ (exp(1)/Γ²)D★ (hence d₀(D, u) = d_u★(T_u^k − 1)^f ≤ D★ exp(−2Cm⁵fL) whenever 1 + 2Cm⁵fL ≤ 2 log Γ) and log X_u − 2 log Γ/(fk) ≤ log T_u ≤ log T_u* + 1 ≤ log X_u + 1.",
      "definitions": [
        "target word scale X_u",
        "lower window endpoint T_u*",
        "combined level modulus M = N(g₀g₁)²",
        "pre-assigned host prime bound X′ = exp(x^(ε/3))",
        "ramified column dimension d₀(D, u) = d_u★(T_u^k − 1)^f"
